---
// Milestone 2 preview: shows the design tokens on each section background.
// Replaced by the real homepage in milestone 3.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Veronica Romero: design operations and people experience leader"
  description="Building the systems and conditions where teams can do their best work."
>
  <section class="section section--teal">
    <div class="container flow" style="--flow-space: var(--space-5)">
      <p class="label">Design operations and people experience leader</p>
      <h1>Veronica Romero</h1>
      <p class="lede">Building the systems and conditions where teams can do their best work.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--paper">
    <div class="container flow">
      <p class="label">Phase 1: Discovery and audit</p>
      <h2>Redefining growth</h2>
      <p>
        I ran 20 sessions with employees, managers, and department leads to find where the
        framework was creating friction, what was missing, and why people weren't using it.
        Alongside that, I audited competency overlap, level progression logic, historical
        promotion feedback, and the language patterns that had piled up over time without
        adding clarity.
      </p>
      <p>
        This is how body text reads on paper. Links look <a href="#main">like this</a>, and
        gaps still waiting on a number look like <span class="todo">[X days]</span>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--mist">
    <div class="container flow">
      <h2>How I work</h2>
      <h3>Turning ambiguity into programs</h3>
      <p>
        I take organizational problems that don't have a shape yet and turn them into
        structured, measurable initiatives. I start with the data, build the case, and design
        toward outcomes I can track.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--teal">
    <div class="container flow">
      <h2>Results</h2>
      <p class="big-number">65%</p>
      <p>of employees had an active growth plan after launch, up from 9%.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--blue">
    <div class="container flow">
      <h2>Reflection</h2>
      <p>
        The biggest challenge was getting a busy organization to stop and engage with it.
        On blue, big numbers and headings stay white, since mustard doesn't have enough
        contrast here.
      </p>
      <p class="big-number">68%</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
